{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs6JwvrSU69ajEqSZ7zM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`get_metadata_for_wheel()` now ignores vendored `.dist-info` directories. All 11 tests in `tests/test_pep658_support.py` pass, including the new ones. I didn't run `hatch run lint:fix` or mypy. `ruff format` isn't installed in `.venv`, so formatting hasn't been checked.\n\n**What changed in `src/fromager/candidate.py`:**\n- It only looks at `.dist-info/METADATA` files in the wheel root, so entries like `pkg/_vendor/other-2.0.dist-info/METADATA` are skipped.\n- If a wheel has more than one root-level `.dist-info`, it picks the one whose name matches the wheel filename in the URL. If none match, it falls back to the first root-level one.\n- I didn't build the exact `{name}-{version}.dist-info/METADATA` path from the issue. The directory name can normalize the version differently from the filename (for example `1.0` vs `1.0.0`), so an exact path could miss a valid wheel.\n\n**New tests in `tests/test_pep658_support.py`:**\n- **Vendored dist-info:** a wheel with a vendored dist-info and a root dist-info, in both zip orders. The root one is returned either way.\n- **Multiple root dist-info dirs:** a wheel with two root-level dist-info directories. The one matching the wheel name is returned."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4024,"cache_read_input_tokens":34778,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4024},"output_tokens":458,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c74ab8ab-6a1c-43bf-9f3f-9c8a153fe34d","uuid":"68a1dc43-5116-4794-b26d-0c70fe76b4f1","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:54:49.034Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs6JwckpKp9bx4VKrzJ5"}
